STAGED PATCH 0002 of 5: apply after 0005.
Target: Linux 6.12.116, mm/slab_common.c. Line anchors are
the patch-point list's numbers of record; context lines are
schematic. Re-base on the real tree before applying.

Subject: iscandar: cache setup at 1.5; krealloc by composition

Creation registers the cache with the layer before the
cache is returned to its creator: an unregistered cache
must never reach 1.1, where an unknown cache after the
raise is a finding. Registration during the prefix is
deferred: the core registers prefix-born caches at the
raise (0005). A registration the layer refuses (the cap)
fails the creation, loudly: the cap is the verdict, and a
kernel that cannot create a cache it was configured to
create has met a build figure that was drawn too small,
which is a finding about the build, not a cue to serve
stock.

Destruction deregisters first; if the layer answers that
objects are still live, the core logs the verdict (0005)
and the stock teardown proceeds, since a cache being
destroyed cannot be undestroyed. The disagreement is on
the record in the log, not papered over.

Center 1.6, krealloc_noprof, takes no hunk in this patch
or any other: it composes an allocation, a copy, and a
free, and 1.1 and 1.4 are patched, so it follows by
composition (reconciliation, Family 1d). Its coverage is
verified by the manifest, not assumed silently.

